Build Trainer and Downloader on Linux

LoRATrainer hands memset optional base addresses, which glibc declares
non-optional, and its largest openStore closure needs an explicit signature
before swiftc 6.0.3 will type-check it in reasonable time. DownloaderSupport
imports CryptoKit and Darwin, so it moves to swift-crypto and a guarded
Glibc, with the CFNetwork and resume-data userInfo key constants written as
their literal strings and a no-op autoreleasepool shim off ObjectiveC.
waitsForConnectivity is get-only in corelibs-foundation.
